msgid "Serial Number"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Every generated SBOM includes a `serialNumber` field in `urn:uuid:` format, "
"as defined by the CycloneDX specification. The serial number is derived from "
"the BOM's content hash, which covers metadata, components, dependency "
"relationships, and other structural fields."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When `project.build.outputTimestamp` is configured in the Maven project (the "
"standard property for https://maven.apache.org/guides/mini/guide-"
"reproducible-builds.html[reproducible builds]), the SBOM metadata timestamp "
"is set to that value, making the entire BOM — including its serial number — "
"fully deterministic across identical builds. Without a reproducible "
"timestamp, the metadata timestamp defaults to the current time, meaning the "
"serial number will vary between builds even if the dependencies have not "
"changed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Product Attribution"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus platforms (such as the Quarkus platform BOM or vendor-provided "
"platforms) may aggregate extensions that belong to commercially supported "
"products, also referred to as _offerings_. When an application is built on "
"such a platform, product attribution represents each supported product as a "
"dedicated component in the generated SBOM and links the application "
"artifacts that belong to that product to it. This lets downstream tools see "
"which parts of an application are covered by a given product and match them "
"against product-level vulnerability and support information, for example by "
"https://nvd.nist.gov/products/cpe[CPE]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Product attribution is enabled by default and applies to every SBOM that "
"includes the core application contribution (dependency, embedded, and "
"distribution SBOMs). It can be disabled with:"
msgstr ""

msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Attribution is driven entirely by metadata the platform provides; an "
"application does not configure products directly. Each imported platform "
"member that declares a product identity (at minimum a CPE) yields, in the "
"generated SBOM, a single product component that:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"has the type `framework` (unless the platform specifies a different type), "
"carries the product's CPE, and has its CycloneDX `scope` set to `excluded`, "
"since the product itself is not a shipped artifact;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"is marked top-level, so it appears as a direct dependency of the main "
"application component;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"_provides_ the artifacts attributed to it — the application's runtime "
"extension artifacts that belong to the product, together with their "
"dependencies. These are recorded as CycloneDX 1.6 `dependency.provides` "
"relationships (the product provides/implements those artifacts). On schema "
"versions older than 1.6, where `provides` is not available, the same "
"artifacts are recorded as `dependsOn` relationships instead."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Platform members that declare the *same* product PURL and CPE are merged "
"into a single product component whose attributed artifacts are the union of "
"the members' contributions. Members with different product PURLs remain "
"separate components even if they share a CPE."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Only artifacts that are actually present in the application and match the "
"coordinates the platform attributed to the product are linked. If the "
"application overrides the version of an attributed dependency, that "
"dependency is not attributed to the product."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A product component is emitted whenever a platform member declares a CPE, "
"even if none of its attributed artifacts end up present in the application."
msgstr ""

msgid "SBOM Component Properties"
msgstr ""

msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Value range"
msgstr ""

msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus:component:scope`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`runtime` or `development`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Indicates whether a component is a runtime or a build/development time "
"dependency of an application. Disabled by default; enable with `quarkus."
"cyclonedx.include-quarkus-component-scope=true`. Development components "
"always have their CycloneDX `scope` set to `excluded` regardless of this "
"setting."
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus:component:location`"
msgstr ""

msgid "String representing a file system path using `/` as a path element"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Used in SBOMs with schema versions 1.4 or older. Starting from schema 1.5, "
"`evidence.occurrences.location` is used instead. This property is used only "
"if a component is found in the distribution. The value is a relative path to "
"a file pointing to the location of a component in a distribution using `/` "
"as a path element separator."
msgstr ""

msgid "Extension SBOM Contributions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, Quarkus generates SBOMs from the application's Maven dependency "
"model and the packaging output.\n"
"Extensions that manage additional software components — for example, npm "
"packages or other non-Maven artifacts — can contribute those components to "
"the application SBOM by producing `SbomContributionBuildItem` instances from "
"their `@BuildStep` methods."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Extension contributions are merged with the core application contribution by "
"the SBOM generator.\n"
"Components marked as top-level will appear as direct dependencies of the "
"main application component in the generated SBOM."
msgstr ""

msgid "API Overview"
msgstr ""

msgid "Extension SBOM contributions are built from the following classes:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`io.quarkus.sbom.Purl` — identifies a software component using the https://"
"github.com/package-url/purl-spec[Package URL] specification. Factory methods "
"are provided for Maven, npm, and generic component types."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`io.quarkus.sbom.ComponentDescriptor` — describes a software component with "
"its PURL, scope, integrity hash, and other metadata."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`io.quarkus.sbom.ComponentDependencies` — describes the dependency "
"relationships of a component, referencing other components by their bom-ref."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`io.quarkus.sbom.SbomContribution` — groups component descriptors and their "
"dependency relationships into a single contribution."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`io.quarkus.deployment.sbom.SbomContributionBuildItem` — a `MultiBuildItem` "
"that carries an `SbomContribution` to the SBOM generator."
msgstr ""

msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The following example shows a `@BuildStep` method that contributes npm "
"packages to the application SBOM:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Key Points"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Extensions must not designate a main component — only the core application "
"contribution does that."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Components from any package ecosystem can be contributed using the "
"appropriate `Purl` type (e.g., `Purl.npm(...)`, `Purl.maven(...)`, `Purl."
"generic(...)`, or `Purl.of(type, ...)` for other ecosystems)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set `topLevel(true)` on components that are direct dependencies of the "
"application (e.g., packages declared in `package.json`). Transitive "
"dependencies should not be marked as top-level."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `scope` field classifies components as `runtime` or `development` "
"dependencies. Development components have their CycloneDX `scope` set to "
"`excluded`. When `quarkus.cyclonedx.include-quarkus-component-scope` is "
"enabled, the scope is also recorded as the `quarkus:component:scope` custom "
"property."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `integrity` field can carry an SRI-format hash (e.g., from lock files) "
"for component verification."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dependency relationships are optional. If you only need to list components "
"without expressing their dependency graph, use `SbomContribution."
"ofComponents(...)`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuration Reference"
msgstr ""
